Piazzolla, Lamothe\u2026","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"pt":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programme d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019Am\u00e9rique latine- oeuvres de Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe\u2026","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"en":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programme dedicated to Latin America - works by Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe,...","shortdescr":"This concert programme is a journey through Latin America, discovering sometimes little-known classical composers. These composers, who come from mixed populations and are influenced by a dual culture, bring to classical music the warmth and vibrancy of their continent.","longdescr":"These composers are Heitor Villa-Lobos, Consuelo Velasquez, Ludovic Lamothe, Mo\u00efses Moleiro, Ernesto Lecuona... All active at the heart of the 20th century, their music reflects human passions, the joy of celebration as much as the tragedy of life.\n\nFrom Brazil to Cuba, Argentina to Venezuela, this recital offers samples of this Latin syncretism between tribal music, dance rhythms and Western classical music.\n\nLike a return to the roots, the recital ends with Spanish composer Manuel de Falla's Fire Dance, emblematic music of a warm and vibrant culture.\n\n \n\nHeitor Villa-Lobos (1887-1959), Brazil\n\nBachianas Brasileira nr 4 for solo piano: Prelude Choros nr 5: Alma Brasileira\n\nChiquinha Gonzaga (1847-1935), Brazil\n\nSospiro\n\nZequinha de Abreu (1880-1935) Brazil\n\nTico tico\n\nErnesto Lecuona (1895-1963), Cuba\n\nLa Comparsa\n\nLudovic Lamothe (1882-1953), Haiti\n\nDanza nr4\n\nMo\u00efses Moleiro (1904-1979), Venezuela\n\nJoropo\n\nOswald Russel (1933-2012), Jamaica\n\nJamaican dance nr 2\n\nAstor Piazzolla (1921-1992), Argentina\n\nLibertango\n\nAdios Nonino\n\nAriel Ramirez (1921-2010), Argentina\n\nAlfonsina y el Mar\n\nConsuelo Velasquez (1919-2005), Mexico\n\nBesame mucho\n\nManuel De Falla (1876-1946) Spain\n\nThe ritual dance of fire\n\nJulie Roz\u00e9 was born in Paris. She began piano and dance at the age of seven at the Boulogne-Billancourt conservatoire, preferring the piano. After studying history, gaining a European master's degree and a variety of professional experiences, she spent two years in Haiti teaching piano at a music school in Jacmel, as part of an international solidarity volunteer programme. On her return to France, she decided to devote herself to the piano and teaching music. Her teacher was Alan Ball. Influenced by her stay in Haiti, she founded the \u2018Bach to Kreyol\u2019 duo with percussionist Claude Saturne, which blends Haitian drum rhythms with classical piano. She holds a French state diploma as a piano teacher and has been teaching in various establishments for fifteen years. She is currently resuming her studies at the Royal Conservatory in Brussels. She recently founded the \u2018Musique Femmes Festival\u2019, dedicated to women composers.\n","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"it":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programme d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019Am\u00e9rique latine- oeuvres de Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe\u2026","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"cn":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programme d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019Am\u00e9rique latine- oeuvres de Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe\u2026","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"fr":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programme d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019Am\u00e9rique latine- oeuvres de Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe\u2026","shortdescr":"Ce programme de concert est un voyage en Am\u00e9rique Latine, \u00e0 la d\u00e9couverte de compositeurs classiques parfois m\u00e9connus. Issus de populations m\u00e9tiss\u00e9es, influenc\u00e9s par une double culture, ces compositeurs apportent \u00e0 la musique classique le souffle chaud et vibrant de leur continent.","longdescr":"Ces compositeurs sont Heitor Villa-Lobos, Consuelo Velasquez, Ludovic Lamothe, Mo\u00efses Moleiro, Ernesto Lecuona\u2026 Tous actifs au c\u0153ur du 20\u00e8 si\u00e8cle, leur musique refl\u00e8te les passions humaines, la joie de la f\u00eate autant que la trag\u00e9die de la vie.\n\nDu Br\u00e9sil \u00e0 Cuba, de l\u2019Argentine au Venezuela, ce r\u00e9cital offre quelques \u00e9chantillons de ce syncr\u00e9tisme latin entre musique tribale, rythmes dansants et musique classique occidentale.\n\nComme un retour aux sources, le r\u00e9cital s\u2019ach\u00e8ve avec la danse du feu du compositeur  espagnol Manuel de Falla, musique embl\u00e9matique d\u2019une culture chaude et vibrante.\n\n \n\nHeitor Villa-Lobos (1887-1959), Br\u00e9sil\n\nBachianas Brasileira nr 4 pour piano solo : Pr\u00e9lude Choros n 5 : Alma Brasileira\n\nChiquinha Gonzaga (1847-1935), Br\u00e9sil\n\nSospiro\n\nZequinha de Abreu (1880-1935) Br\u00e9sil\n\nTico tico\n\nErnesto Lecuona (1895-1963), Cuba\n\nLa Comparsa\n\nLudovic Lamothe (1882-1953), Ha\u00efti\n\nDanza nr4\n\nMo\u00efses Moleiro (1904-1979), V\u00e9n\u00e9zuela\n\nJoropo\n\nOswald Russel (1933-2012), Jama\u00efque\n\nJamaican dance nr 2\n\nAstor Piazzolla (1921-1992), Argentine\n\nLibertango\n\nAdios Nonino\n\nAriel Ramirez (1921-2010), Argentine\n\nAlfonsina y el Mar\n\nConsuelo Velasquez (1919-2005) Mexique\n\nBesame mucho\n\nManuel De Falla (1876-1946) Espagne\n\nLa danse rituelle du feu\n\n \n\nJulie Roz\u00e9 est n\u00e9e \u00e0 Paris. Elle commence le piano et la danse \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e2ge de sept ans au conservatoire de Boulogne-Billancourt et privil\u00e9gie le piano. Apr\u00e8s des \u00e9tudes d\u2019Histoire, un master europ\u00e9en et diverses exp\u00e9riences professionnelles, elle part deux ans en Ha\u00efti enseigner le piano dans une \u00e9cole de musique \u00e0 Jacmel, dans le cadre d\u2019un volontariat de solidarit\u00e9 internationale. A son retour en France, elle d\u00e9cide de se consacrer au piano et \u00e0 l\u2019enseignement de la musique. Elle a comme professeur Alan Ball. Influenc\u00e9e par son s\u00e9jour en Ha\u00efti, elle fonde le duo \u201cBach to Kreyol\u201d, avec le percussionniste Claude Saturne, qui m\u00eale rythmes ha\u00eftiens au tambour et piano classique. Elle est titulaire du dipl\u00f4me d\u2019Etat Fran\u00e7ais de professeur de piano et enseigne dans diverses structures depuis quinze ans. Elle est actuellement en reprise d\u2019\u00e9tudes au conservatoire royal de Bruxelles. Elle a r\u00e9cemment fond\u00e9 le \u201cMusique Femmes Festival\u201d, d\u00e9di\u00e9 aux compositrices.\n\n ","performers":"Julie Roz\u00e9 (piano)","boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"sp":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programme d\u00e9di\u00e9 \u00e0 l\u2019Am\u00e9rique latine- oeuvres de Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe\u2026","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"},"nl":{"name":"Julie Roz\u00e9, piano solo: programma gewijd aan Latijns-Amerika - werken van Villa-Lobos, Piazzolla, Lamothe...","shortdescr":"Dit concertprogramma is een reis door Latijns-Amerika, waarbij soms weinig bekende klassieke componisten worden ontdekt. Deze componisten, afkomstig uit gemengde bevolkingsgroepen en be\u00efnvloed door een dubbele cultuur, bezielen de klassieke muziek met de warmte en levendigheid van hun continent.\n","longdescr":"Deze componisten zijn Heitor Villa-Lobos, Consuelo Velasquez, Ludovic Lamothe, Mo\u00efses Moleiro, Ernesto Lecuona... Allen actief in het hart van de 20e eeuw, weerspiegelt hun muziek menselijke passies, zowel de vreugde van het feest als de tragedie van het leven.\n\nVan Brazili\u00eb tot Cuba, van Argentini\u00eb tot Venezuela, biedt dit recital voorbeelden van dit Latijns syncretisme tussen tribale muziek, dansritmes en Westerse klassieke muziek.\n\nAls een terugkeer naar de wortels wordt het recital afgesloten met de Vuurdans van de Spaanse componist Manuel de Falla, emblematische muziek van een warme en levendige cultuur.\n\n \n\nHeitor Villa-Lobos (1887-1959), Brazili\u00eb\n\nBachianas Brasileira nr 4 voor piano solo: Prelude Choros nr 5: Alma Brasileira\n\nChiquinha Gonzaga (1847-1935), Brazili\u00eb\n\nSospiro\n\nZequinha de Abreu (1880-1935) Brazili\u00eb\n\nTico tico\n\nErnesto Lecuona (1895-1963), Cuba\n\nLa Comparsa\n\nLudovic Lamothe (1882-1953), Ha\u00efti\n\nDanza nr4\n\nMo\u00efses Moleiro (1904-1979), Venezuela\n\nJoropo\n\nOswald Russel (1933-2012), Jamaica\n\nJamaicaanse dans nr 2\n\nAstor Piazzolla (1921-1992), Argentini\u00eb\n\nLibertango\n\nAdios Nonino\n\nAriel Ramirez (1921-2010), Argentini\u00eb\n\nAlfonsina en de zee\n\nConsuelo Velasquez (1919-2005), Mexico\n\nVeel groeten\n\nManuel De Falla (1876-1946) Spanje\n\nDe rituele dans van het vuur\n\nJulie Roz\u00e9 werd geboren in Parijs. Ze begon op zevenjarige leeftijd met piano en dans aan het conservatorium van Boulogne-Billancourt, waarbij haar voorkeur uitging naar de piano. Na een studie geschiedenis, een Europese master en verschillende professionele ervaringen, bracht ze twee jaar door in Ha\u00efti als pianolerares aan een muziekschool in Jacmel, in het kader van een vrijwilligersprogramma voor internationale solidariteit. Bij haar terugkeer in Frankrijk besloot ze zich toe te wijden aan de piano en het muziekonderwijs. Haar leraar was Alan Ball. Onder invloed van haar verblijf in Ha\u00efti richtte ze samen met percussionist Claude Saturne het duo \u201cBach to Kreyol\u201d op, dat Ha\u00eftiaanse drumritmes combineert met klassieke piano. Ze heeft een Frans staatsdiploma als pianolerares en geeft al vijftien jaar les in verschillende instellingen. Momenteel hervat ze haar studies aan het Koninklijk Conservatorium in Brussel. Onlangs richtte ze het \u201cMusique Femmes Festival\u201d op, gewijd aan vrouwelijke componisten.\n\n\n ","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/agenda\/2025-03-22-julie-roze-piano-solo\/","email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700007739"}},"place":{"id":242272,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Atelier Marcel Hastir ist ein Ort der Kunst, der kulturellen und k\u00fcnstlerischen Begegnungen, der 1935 von dem Maler Marcel Hastir in seinem K\u00fcnstleratelier in der Rue du Commerce 51 eingerichtet wurde. Das ungew\u00f6hnliche Haus hei\u00dft seit Jahrzehnten inmitten der Kunstwerke sowohl junge K\u00fcnstler als auch gro\u00dfe Namen der belgischen und internationalen Musik- und Theaterszene willkommen - ein Ort, der mit seiner ganz besonderen Atmosph\u00e4re verzaubert.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Handelsstraat","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Handelsstraat, 51","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"The Atelier Marcel Hastir is a magical place where culture lovers and artists meet in the midst of Marcel Hastir's paintings, in the intimate setting of what has been his place of work since 1935.\r\nMarcel Hastir was a Belgian painter, theosofist and resistance fighter. His studio in the Leopold district served also as a concert hall for young musicians, and during the Second World War this \"painters school\" actually served as a relatively safe meeting place for young artists, students and resistance fighters. A team of passionate volunteers work for the preservation of his work and home organising concerts with both young and confirmed talent from Belgium and abroad.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Atelier Marcel Hastir","address_street_name":"Rue du Commerce","address_street_number":"51","address_street_box":null,"email":"ateliermarcelhastir@gmail.com","website":"http:\/\/ateliermarcelhastir.eu\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue du Commerce, 51","add