210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Place Charles Rogier, 11","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Belfius Art Gallery","address_street_name":"Place Charles Rogier","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"artcollection@belfius.be","website":"http:\/\/www.belfius-art-collection.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Place Charles Rogier, 11","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Belfius Art Gallery","address_street_name":"Place Charles Rogier","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"artcollection@belfius.be","website":"http:\/\/www.belfius-art-collection.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Place Charles Rogier, 11","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Belfius Art Gallery","address_street_name":"Place Charles Rogier","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"artcollection@belfius.be","website":"http:\/\/www.belfius-art-collection.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Place Charles Rogier, 11","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":"La collection Belfius est la plus grande collection d\u2019art belge du pays. La collection compte plus de 4 300 \u0153uvres d\u2019art et r\u00e9sulte de la fusion des collections du Cr\u00e9dit communal de Belgique, de Paribas Banque Belgique et de BACOB Banque.\r\n\r\nApr\u00e8s la Deuxi\u00e8me Guerre Mondiale, tant le Cr\u00e9dit communal que Paribas Belgique ont commenc\u00e9 \u00e0 acqu\u00e9rir des \u0153uvres de grande valeur li\u00e9es \u00e0 l\u2019h\u00e9ritage national belge, afin d\u2019\u00e9viter qu\u2019elles ne disparaissent \u00e0 l\u2019\u00e9tranger. D\u00e8s le d\u00e9but, le Cr\u00e9dit communal a mis l\u2019accent sur l\u2019art belge \u00e0 partir de 1860, tandis que Paribas se concentrait principalement sur des \u0153uvres du 16e au 18e si\u00e8cle et sur l\u2019art contemporain. BACOB banque a commenc\u00e9 sa collection en 1980 et s\u2019est exclusivement consacr\u00e9e \u00e0 l\u2019art contemporain belge. Aujourd\u2019hui, la collection couvre pr\u00e8s de cinq si\u00e8cles.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Belfius Art Gallery","address_street_name":"Place Charles Rogier","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"artcollection@belfius.be","website":"http:\/\/www.belfius-art-collection.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","address_line1":"Place Charles Rogier, 11","address_line2":"1210 Saint-Josse-Ten-Noode","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Belfius Art Gallery","address_street_name":"Charles Rogierplein","address_street_number":"11","address_street_box":null,"email":"artcollection@belfius.be","website":"http:\/\/www.belfius-art-collection.be","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1210","address_city":"Sint-Joost-Ten-Node","address_line1":"Charles Rogierplein, 11","address_line2":"1210 Sint-Joost-Ten-Node","description_web":"De Belfius-kunstcollectie is de grootste verzameling van Belgische kunst van het land en omvat meer dan 4300 werken, het gevolg van de samensmelting van de kunstverzamelingen van het Gemeentekrediet, Paribas Bank Belgi\u00eb en BACOB Bank.\r\n\r\nZowel het Gemeentekrediet als Paribas Belgi\u00eb begonnen na de Tweede Wereldoorlog met het verzamelen van waardevolle kunstwerken uit het nationaal erfgoed om te vermijden dat ze naar het buitenland verdwenen. Het Gemeentekrediet legde van in het begin het accent op Belgische kunst vanaf 1860, terwijl Paribas Belgi\u00eb kunst uit de 16de tot de 18de eeuw en moderne kunst kocht. BACOB bank begon zijn verzameling in 1980 en legde zich uitsluitend toe op Belgische hedendaagse kunst. Vandaag bestrijkt de collectie werken uit bijna vijf eeuwen.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[15],"translations":{"de":["Rogier"],"pt":[null],"en":["Rogier"],"it":["Rogier"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Rogier"],"sp":["Rogier"],"nl":["Rogier"]}},"zones":{"list":[20],"translations":{"de":["Norden"],"pt":[null],"en":["North"],"it":["Nord"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Nord"],"sp":["Norte"],"nl":["Noord"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":26601,"location":{"lat":50.8565062,"lon":4.3594062},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-06-06T16:33:40+02:00","published_at":"2016-10-14T09:55:01+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":276946,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be\/en","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Since 1983, Arkadia has been exploring the richness of Belgium's and Brussels' heritage and developing numerous cultural projects especially in Brussels, between architecture, urbanism, culture, plastic arts and ideology from the Middle Ages to the present day. Seeing and understanding the city and its architectural development, approaching artistic creation and giving it meaning, these are the activities that the ASBL wants to share with the public. Specialists in architectural heritage and contemporary art, they show the city through guided tours and lectures in several languages.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Depuis 1983, Arkadia explore les richesses du patrimoine belge et bruxellois et d\u00e9veloppe de nombreux projets culturels sp\u00e9cialement \u00e0 Bruxelles, entre architecture, urbanisme, culture, arts plastiques et id\u00e9ologie depuis le Moyen \u00c2ge jusqu\u2019\u00e0 nos jours. Voir et comprendre la ville et son d\u00e9veloppement architectural, approcher la cr\u00e9ation artistique et lui donner un sens, telles sont les activit\u00e9s que l'ASBL veut partager avec le public. Sp\u00e9cialistes du patrimoine  architectural et de l'art contemporain, ils font d\u00e9couvrir la ville \u00e0 travers des visites guid\u00e9es et des conf\u00e9rences en plusieurs langues.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Rue de Namur","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Rue de Namur, 10","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Arkadia","address_street_name":"Naamsestraat","address_street_number":"10","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@arkadia.be","website":"https:\/\/arkadia.be\/nl","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 45 60","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Naamsestraat, 10","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Sinds 1983 verkent Arkadia de rijkdom van het Belgische en Brusselse erfgoed en ontwikkelt talrijke culturele projecten, vooral in Brussel, tussen architectuur, stedenbouw, cultuur, plastische kunsten en ideologie, van de Middeleeuwen tot vandaag. De stad en haar architecturale ontwikkeling zien en begrijpen, de artistieke creatie benaderen en er een betekenis aan geven, dat zijn de activiteiten die de VZW met het publiek wil delen. Zij zijn gespecialiseerd in architectonisch erfgoed en hedendaagse kunst en laten de stad zien door middel van rondleidingen en lezingen in verschillende talen.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":36946,"location":{"lat":50.84145283,"lon":4.35976257},"last_updated_at":"2023-06-08T12:25:28+02:00","published_at":"2021-07-23T14:48:31+02:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/8accbc83ad19889d752f97db131d49e06bff2238.jpeg","width":1280,"height":853,"ratio":1.5,"oEmbed_height":853,"oEmbed_width":1280,"translations":{"de":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"pt":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"en":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"it":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"cn":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"fr":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"sp":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"},"nl":{"title":"Art Pops - Belfius Art Gallery","copyright":"\u00a9Thibault de Lestr\u00e9"}}}],"dates":[{"day":"2025-01-11","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-02-01","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-02-15","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":true,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-02-15","doors":null,"start":"14:30:00","end":"15:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-03-08","doors":null,"start":"14:30:00","end":"15:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-03-08","doors":null,"start":"16:00:00","end":"17:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-03-22","doors":null,"start":"14:30:00","end":"15:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-03-22","doors":null,"start":"16:00:00","end":"17:00:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-04-05","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-04-05","doors":null,"start":"14:30:00","end":"15:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-04-26","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-05-17","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false},{"day":"2025-06-21","doors":null,"start":"11:30:00","end":"12:30:00","end_night_life":null,"is_soldout":false,"is_canceled":false}],"prices":[{"translations":{"de":{"name":"Normal"},"en":{"name":"Normal"},"it":{"name":"Normale"},"fr":{"name":"Normal"},"sp":{"name":"Normal"},"nl":{"name":"Normaal"}},"value":12}],"date_exceptions":[],"closing_days":[],"child_events":[],"parent_events":[],"accessibilities":[],"recurring":[],"targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"educational_targets":{"list":[],"translations":{}},"tags":[]},{"id":50011322,"date_start":"2024-05-25","date_end":"2025-05-25","date_next":"2025-03-22","accept_article27":false,"accept_cultuurbon":false,"accept_paspartoe":false,"is_closed_on_public_holidays":false,"is_closed_on_school_holidays":false,"is_only_by_appointment":false,"is_permanent":false,"is_free":false,"is_pay_as_you_can":false,"is_online":false,"is_canceled":false,"is_soldout":false,"last_updated_at":"2025-03-21T12:37:32+01:00","published_at":"2024-06-04T13:00:21+02:00","publication_state":"public","date_embargo":null,"show_in_agenda":true,"is_outside":false,"is_high_capacity":false,"is_not_major_event":false,"backoffice_id":301394,"facebook_link":null,"import_origin":null,"is_part_of":"\u00c9v\u00e9nement Art nouveau","sub_type":"expo","ranking":0.17613661133226788,"languages":{"spoken":["nl","de","fr","en"],"subtitles":[]},"categories":{"main":{"id":23,"translations":{"de":"Ausstellung","pt":null,"en":"Exhibitions","it":"Esposizioni","cn":null,"fr":"Expositions","sp":"Exposici\u00f3n","nl":"Tentoonstellingen"}},"others":{"list":[48,36],"translations":{"de":["Architektur","Museen & Kunstzentren"],"pt":[null,null],"en":["Architecture ","Museums and art centers"],"it":["Architettura","Musei e centri artistici"],"cn":[null,null],"fr":["Architecture","Mus\u00e9es et art centers"],"sp":["Arquitectura","Museos y centros de arte"],"nl":["Architectuur","Musea en kunstcentra"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"pt":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"en":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution is now on show at LAB\u00b7AN x Hotel van Eetvelde, following its debut at the Art and History Museum in Brussels. The exhibition presents a never-before-seen digital reconstruction of the interiors as they looked around 1911. It's a unique opportunity to explore the remarkable d\u00e9cor of this building, which has been on UNESCO's World Heritage List since 2009.","longdescr":"Result of a collaboration between urban.brussels, the ULB - Architecture Faculty La Cambre Horta and the Art & History Museum, initiated to mark the Brussels Art Nouveau Year 2023, this exhibition and the digital reconstruction presented in the form of a film are designed to enable visitors to explore the interiors of the Palais Stoclet, which has been on the very select list of Brussels buildings included on UNESCO's World Heritage List since 2009, and yet is still little known to the general public.\n\nThe virtual reconstruction of this palace (which reproduces the state of the palace between 1911 and 1918 and does not represent the existing situation) is based on precise archival sources and a detailed architectural analysis of its spaces, a task that kept the ULB team of experts busy for almost two years. This scientific study of the Stoclet Palace is part of a close collaboration between experts from the Brussels-Capital Region (Urban.brussels) and ULB (alICe Laboratory). Its realism reinforces the impression that visitors are being immersed in the building's original state, between 1911 and 1918: the public is discovering the palace exactly as the couple Suzanne Stevens and Adolphe Stoclet dreamed it would be.\n\nThrough this research, the Brussels Region hopes not only to make this knowledge accessible to as many people as possible, but also to build up a scientific information base on the spatial nature of the building and its remarkable decorations. Behind this digital documentation project, the research carried out by the AlICe laboratory at the Faculty of Architecture (ULB) aims to consolidate a knowledge base around the three-dimensional representation of the building, which will be enriched over time. The digitisation of the floors, service areas and gardens of the Palais Stoclet will be added to the work already carried out. The work of reconstituting the original art collection will also continue, so that this digital double of the building can gradually be reintegrated.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"it":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"cn":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"fr":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":"Apr\u00e8s avoir \u00e9t\u00e9 pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e au Mus\u00e9e d'Art et d'Histoire de Bruxelles, Stoclet 1911 - Restitution s'invite au LAB\u00b7AN x Hotel van Eetvelde. L'exposition pr\u00e9sente une reconstitution num\u00e9rique in\u00e9dite de ses int\u00e9rieurs tels qu\u2019ils se pr\u00e9sentaient vers 1911. Une occasion unique de parcourir les d\u00e9cors remarquables de cet \u00e9difice inscrit depuis 2009 sur la Liste du Patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO.\n","longdescr":"Fruit d\u2019une collaboration entre urban.brussels, l\u2019ULB \u2013 Facult\u00e9 d\u2019Architecture La Cambre Horta et le Mus\u00e9e Art & Histoire, initi\u00e9e \u00e0 l\u2019occasion de l\u2019ann\u00e9e Art Nouveau Brussels 2023, cette exposition et la reconstitution num\u00e9rique qui est pr\u00e9sent\u00e9e sous forme de film ont pour ambition de permettre aux visiteurs de parcourir les int\u00e9rieurs du palais Stoclet, inscrit sur la liste tr\u00e8s ferm\u00e9e des quelques b\u00e2timents bruxellois repris au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO, depuis 2009, et pourtant encore peu connu du grand public.\n\nLa reconstitution virtuelle de ce palais (qui reproduit l\u2019\u00e9tat du palais entre 1911 et 1918 et qui ne repr\u00e9sente pas la situation existante) est bas\u00e9e sur des sources archivistiques pr\u00e9cises puis sur une analyse architecturale fine de ses espaces ; un travail qui a occup\u00e9 pendant presque deux ans l\u2019\u00e9quipe d\u2019experts de l'ULB. Cette \u00e9tude scientifique du palais Stoclet s\u2019inscrit en effet dans le cadre d\u2019une collaboration \u00e9troite entre les experts de la R\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale (Urban.brussels) et l\u2019ULB (Laboratoire alICe). Son r\u00e9alisme renforce l\u2019impression d\u2019immersion des visiteurs dans un \u00e9tat d\u2019origine du b\u00e2timent, entre 1911 et 1918 : le public d\u00e9couvre le palais exactement comme l\u2019ont r\u00eav\u00e9 le couple Suzanne Stevens et Adolphe Stoclet.\n\n\u00c0 travers cette recherche, la R\u00e9gion bruxelloise souhaite non seulement rendre cette connaissance accessible au plus grand nombre, mais aussi construire une base d\u2019information scientifique sur la spatialit\u00e9 du b\u00e2timent et ses d\u00e9cors remarquables. Derri\u00e8re ce projet de documentation num\u00e9rique, la recherche conduite par le laboratoire AlICe de la Facult\u00e9 d\u2019architecture (ULB) entend consolider, autour de la repr\u00e9sentation tridimensionnelle de l\u2019\u00e9difice, une base de connaissances qui sera enrichie dans le temps. La num\u00e9risation des \u00e9tages, des espaces de service et des jardins du palais Stoclet viendront s\u2019ajouter au travail d\u00e9j\u00e0 effectu\u00e9. Et dans le prolongement, le travail de reconstitution de la collection d\u2019art d\u2019origine se poursuivra de mani\u00e8re \u00e0 r\u00e9int\u00e9grer progressivement ce double num\u00e9rique de l\u2019\u00e9difice.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"sp":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"},"nl":{"name":"Stoclet 1911 - Reconstructie","shortdescr":"Stoclet 1911 - Restitution is nu te zien in LAB-AN x Hotel van Eetvelde, na het debuut in het Museum Kunst en Geschiedenis in Brussel. De tentoonstelling toont een nooit eerder vertoonde digitale reconstructie van de interieurs zoals ze er rond 1911 uitzagen. Het is een unieke kans om de opmerkelijke inrichting van dit gebouw, dat sinds 2009 op de Werelderfgoedlijst van UNESCO staat, te ontdekken.","longdescr":"Deze tentoonstelling is het resultaat van een samenwerking tussen urban.brussels, vzw Patrimoine & Culture, de architectuurfaculteit La Cambre Horta van de ULB en het Museum Kunst & Geschiedenis, opgezet ter gelegenheid van het jaar Art Nouveau Brussels 2023. Ze zijn bedoeld om bezoekers de interieurs van het Palais Stoclet te laten ontdekken, dat sinds 2009 op de zeer selecte lijst van Brusselse gebouwen staat die op de Werelderfgoedlijst van UNESCO staan, maar nog weinig bekend is bij het grote publiek.\n\nDe virtuele reconstructie van dit paleis (die de toestand van het paleis tussen 1911 en 1918 reproduceert en niet de bestaande situatie weergeeft) is gebaseerd op nauwkeurige archiefbronnen en een gedetailleerde architecturale analyse van de ruimtes, een taak die het team van deskundigen van de ULB bijna twee jaar heeft beziggehouden. Deze wetenschappelijke studie van het Stocletpaleis kadert in een nauwe samenwerking tussen de deskundigen van het Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest (Urban.brussels) en de ULB (Laboratorium alICe). Het realisme versterkt de indruk dat bezoekers ondergedompeld worden in de oorspronkelijke staat van het gebouw, tussen 1911 en 1918: het publiek ontdekt het paleis precies zoals het echtpaar Suzanne Stevens en Adolphe Stoclet het droomde.\n\nMet dit onderzoek wil het Brussels Gewest niet alleen deze kennis toegankelijk maken voor zoveel mogelijk mensen, maar ook een wetenschappelijke databank opbouwen over de ruimtelijke aard van het gebouw en zijn opmerkelijke decoraties. Achter dit digitale documentatieproject schuilt het onderzoek van het laboratorium AlICe van de Faculteit Architectuur (ULB) om een kennisbasis te consolideren rond de driedimensionale voorstelling van het gebouw, die in de loop van de tijd zal worden verrijkt. De digitalisering van de verdiepingen, dienstruimten en tuinen van het Palais Stoclet zal worden toegevoegd aan het reeds uitgevoerde werk. De reconstructie van de originele kunstcollectie zal ook worden voortgezet, zodat deze digitale dubbelganger van het gebouw geleidelijk aan opnieuw kan worden ge\u00efntegreerd.","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","email":"info@lab-an.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 303 48 94","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.50011322"}},"place":{"id":242040,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Das Maison van Eetvelde ist ein bemerkenswertes Jugendstilbauwerk aus der Feder von Victor Horta, das 1895-1898 im Auftrag des Diplomaten Edmond Van Eetvelde erbaut wurde. Das Geb\u00e4ude z\u00e4hlt zum UNESCO-Weltkulturerbe.\r\n\r\nDas Geb\u00e4ude wurde 1895 von Edmond Van Eetvelde, seinerzeit Diplomat und Generalsekret\u00e4r im Kongo, in Auftrag gegeben. Sehenswert sind die Eisentr\u00e4ger aus Flacheisen (wie im Industriebereich) statt aus Schmiedeeisen, die Mosaike, der glas\u00fcberdachte Innenhof und die Blumenmotive des Esszimmers.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Palmerstonlaan","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Palmerstonlaan, 2","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"Created in 2023 to celebrate the 130th anniversary of the birth of Art Nouveau in Brussels, the LAB\u00b7AN (Laboratory Art Nouveau) aims to enhance and promote this unique style and the general and specific themes associated with it. Through its exhibitions and activities, it takes a contemporary look at this Belgian, Brussels and international cultural heritage.\nLAB\u00b7AN is located in the van Eetvelde building, one of Victor Horta's finest creations and a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The opening of LAB\u00b7AN in this extraordinary building makes the Hotel van Eetvelde, a jewel of Brussels Art Nouveau, accessible to the general public 3 days a week.\nThe LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde project is managed by the non-profit organisation Patrimoine & Culture, which is also responsible for managing the Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry.\n","description_print":"According to Horta himself, the plans for this house, conceived in 1895, were the most audacious he ever drew. And he did so for a prominent figure, as the client, Baron Edmond van Eetvelde, was the Secretary General of the Independent State of Congo - in reality the unofficial 'Minister of the Congo' - and, therefore, a very close ally of King Leopold II. \n\nThe future owner asked the architect for a house 'for his family', but with as large a living room and dining room as possible, given his frequent social engagements. \n\nThe house is unusual in that it is flanked by two other buildings: a building to the left of it, which was intended to serve both as an extension to the original house and as a rental house and a building to the right of it, a small annex to the main house. ","booking_url":"https:\/\/shop.utick.be\/?pos=LABAN&module=ACTIVITYSERIEDETAILS&s=E4D8C982-7620-86BE-07B4-22D6FF0EFE20&lg=EN","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Hotel van Eetvelde & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Cr\u00e9\u00e9 en 2023 pour c\u00e9l\u00e9brer le 130e anniversaire de la naissance de l'Art nouveau \u00e0 Bruxelles, le LAB\u00b7AN (Laboratoire Art nouveau) a pour mission de valoriser et de promouvoir ce style unique et les th\u00e8mes g\u00e9n\u00e9raux et sp\u00e9cifiques qui lui sont associ\u00e9s. \u00c0 travers les expositions et activit\u00e9s qu'il propose, il pose un regard contemporain sur cet h\u00e9ritage culturel belge, bruxellois et international. \nLe LAB\u00b7AN est situ\u00e9 au sein du b\u00e2timent van Eetvelde, l\u2019une des plus belles cr\u00e9ations de Victor Horta, class\u00e9e au patrimoine mondial de l\u2019UNESCO. L\u2019ouverture du LAB\u00b7AN dans ce b\u00e2timent extraordinaire rend l\u2019H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde, joyau de l\u2019Art nouveau bruxellois, accessible au grand public 3 jours par semaine.\nLe projet LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde est g\u00e9r\u00e9 par l\u2019asbl Patrimoine & Culture, \u00e9galement responsable des Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry.\n","description_print":"28\/10\/24 Selon les dires de Horta lui-m\u00eame, le plan de cette maison, con\u00e7u en 1895, est le plus audacieux qu\u2019il ait dessin\u00e9\u2026 Et c\u2019est encore au profit d\u2019une personnalit\u00e9 qu\u2019il le fait, puisque le commanditaire, le baron Edmond van Eetvelde, est le secr\u00e9taire g\u00e9n\u00e9ral de l\u2019\u00c9tat ind\u00e9pendant du Congo \u2014 dans les faits v\u00e9ritable \u00ab ministre du Congo \u00bb \u2014, et donc un tr\u00e8s proche collaborateur du roi L\u00e9opold II. \n\nLe futur propri\u00e9taire r\u00e9clame \u00e0 l\u2019architecte une maison \u00ab pour sa famille \u00bb, mais comportant, au vu de ses obligations mondaines, un salon et une salle \u00e0 manger aussi grands que possible. \n\nLa maison offre la particularit\u00e9 d\u2019\u00eatre flanqu\u00e9e de deux autres \u00e9difices, de part et d\u2019autre : un immeuble \u00e0 sa gauche, devant \u00e0 la fois servir d\u2019agrandissement \u00e0 la maison initiale et de maison de location ; un b\u00e2timent \u00e0 sa droite, petite annexe \u00e0 l\u2019habitation principale. ","booking_url":"https:\/\/shop.utick.be\/?pos=LABAN&module=ACTIVITYSERIEDETAILS&s=E4D8C982-7620-86BE-07B4-22D6FF0EFE20&lg=FR","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Van Eetvelde Hotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Avenue Palmerston","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Avenue Palmerston, 2","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Van Eetveldehotel & LAB\u00b7An","address_street_name":"Palmerstonlaan","address_street_number":"2","address_street_box":null,"email":"team@lab-an.be","website":"https:\/\/www.lab-an.be\/","phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Palmerstonlaan, 2","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"Het LAB\u00b7AN (Laboratorium art nouveau) werd opgericht in 2023 om de 130ste verjaardag van de geboorte van de art nouveau in Brussel te vieren en heeft als doel deze unieke stijl en de algemene en specifieke thema's die ermee verbonden zijn, te valoriseren en te promoten. Door middel van tentoonstellingen en activiteiten biedt het een hedendaagse kijk op dit Belgische, Brusselse en internationale culturele erfgoed.\nLAB\u00b7AN is gevestigd in het van Eetvelde gebouw, een van de mooiste creaties van Victor Horta en UNESCO-werelderfgoed. De opening van LAB\u00b7AN in dit buitengewone gebouw maakt het Hotel van Eetvelde, een juweel van de Brusselse art nouveau, 3 dagen per week toegankelijk voor het grote publiek.\nHet project LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel van Eetvelde wordt beheerd door de vzw Patrimoine & Culture, die ook verantwoordelijk is voor het beheer van de Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry.\n","description_print":"Volgens Victor Horta zelf was het plan voor dit huis in 1895 het meest gedurfde dat hij ooit had ontworpen. De opdrachtgever was ook niet de eerste de beste: baron Edmond van Eetvelde was de secretaris-generaal van de onafhankelijke staat Congo - de 'minister van Congo', zeg maar - en dus een zeer naaste medewerker van koning Leopold II. \n\nDe toekomstige eigenaar vroeg de architect om een huis \u2018voor zijn gezin,\u2019 maar met een zo groot mogelijke woonkamer en eetkamer met het oog op zijn sociale verplichtingen. \n\nBijzonder is dat het huis in feite een drie-eenheid is. Het wordt geflankeerd door twee andere gebouwen: een gebouw links van het huis, dat zowel als uitbreiding van het oorspronkelijke huis als als huurhuis moest dienen, en een gebouw rechts van het huis, een klein bijgebouw bij het hoofdhuis. ","booking_url":"https:\/\/shop.utick.be\/?pos=LABAN&module=ACTIVITYSERIEDETAILS&s=E4D8C982-7620-86BE-07B4-22D6FF0EFE20&lg=NL","sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"de":["Europ\u00e4isches Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["European Quarter"],"it":["Quartiere europeo"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"sp":["Barrio Europeo"],"nl":["Europese wijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"de":["Osten"],"pt":[null],"en":["East"],"it":["Est"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Est"],"sp":["Este"],"nl":["Oost"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":4486,"location":{"lat":50.8472189,"lon":4.3803579},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2024-10-28T12:06:41+01:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:17:26+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":247371,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Die Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry mit ihrer eklektischen Architektur wurden Ende des 19. Jahrhundert als Markthalle erbaut und spielten in der Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgeschichte eine wichtige Rolle.\r\n\r\nDie Saint-G\u00e9ry-Hallen waren einerseits sowohl legend\u00e4re als auch kaufm\u00e4nnische Wiege der Stadt. Ab dem 11. Jahrhundert stand an dieser Stelle eine dem Heiligen Saint-G\u00e9ry gewidmete Kapelle. Verschiedene Wohnh\u00e4user waren hier entstanden und aufgrund der N\u00e4he zur Senne entwickelten sich zahlreiche Aktivit\u00e4ten.\r\n\r\nIm 16. Jahrhundert erhielt die Kapelle den Status einer Pfarrkirche, die prachtvoll im gotischen Stil erweitert wurde, dann aber im Zuge der Franz\u00f6sische Revolution dem Erdboden gleichgemacht wurde.\r\n\r\nDer ehemalige Markt - und sogar das gesamte Saint-G\u00e9ry-Viertel \u2013 waren ihrerseits in den 1960er-Jahren von der Zerst\u00f6rung bedroht, bis das Viertel in den 1990er-Jahren eine Art zweiten Fr\u00fchling erlebte. Seit 1999 fungieren die Saint-G\u00e9ry-Hallen als Informations- und Ausstellungszentrum rund um die Br\u00fcsseler Stadtgeschichte und das st\u00e4dtische Leben in Br\u00fcssel. An der Bar gibt es Getr\u00e4nke und Speisen.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussels","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Brussels","description_web":"The Saint-G\u00e9ry Market Halls are a fine architectural example of 19th-century public markets in Brussels. The building was completely restored several years ago and is now a permanent information and exhibition space, with urban planning, heritage, and urban renewal as its central themes.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Halle di Saint-Gery","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Le Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry (mercato coperto) ospitano un centro d'informazione dedicato al patrimonio e al quadro di vita dei Bruxellesi...\r\nLe Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry (mercato coperto) ospitano un centro d'informazione dedicato al patrimonio e al quadro di vita dei Bruxellesi. Sotto il patrocinio della regione di Bruxelles Capitale.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Remarquable t\u00e9moin de l\u2019architecture des march\u00e9s couverts, les Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry  contribuent \u00e0 valoriser le patrimoine de la R\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale. Centre d\u2019exposition et de manifestation bas\u00e9 en plein coeur du pentagone, elles ont pour vocation de mettre en valeur les traits de d\u00e9marcation du cadre de vie bruxellois et de son identit\u00e9 urbaine par le biais d'une programmation hybride, allant des expositions, aux conf\u00e9rences, concerts, rencontres et performances \u2026\r\nLe Centre Urbain (guichet d\u2019information r\u00e9gional, pour mieux vous conseiller sur l\u2019habitat durable en R\u00e9gion de Bruxelles-Capitale) est \u00e9galement situ\u00e9 au sein des Halles.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_name":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Bruxelles","address_line1":"Place Saint-G\u00e9ry","address_line2":"1000 Bruxelles","description_web":"Verdadero testigo de los mercados cubiertos, las Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry albergan un centro de informaci\u00f3n, bajo la \u00e9gida de la Regio\u00f3n de Bruselas Capital y dedicado al patrimonio...\r\nVerdadero testigo de los mercados cubiertos, las Halles Saint-G\u00e9ry albergan un centro de informaci\u00f3n, bajo la \u00e9gida de la Regio\u00f3n de Bruselas Capital y dedicado al patrimonio y al marco de vida de los bruselenses.\r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Sint-Gorikshallen","address_street_name":"Sint-Goriksplein","address_street_number":null,"address_street_box":null,"email":"accueil@hallessaintgery.be","website":"http:\/\/www.hallessaintgery.be","phone_contact":"+32 2 502 44 24","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1000","address_city":"Brussel","address_line1":"Sint-Goriksplein","address_line2":"1000 Brussel","description_web":"De Sint-Gorikshallen zijn een prachtig architecturaal staaltje van openbare markthallen in het 19de-eeuwse Brussel. Het gebouw werd een aantal jaren geleden volledig gerestaureerd en doet tegenwoordig dienst als permanente informatie-, tentoonstellings- en evenementenruimte gewijd aan het erfgoed en de levenswijzen in de hoofdstad. Op amper twee minuten stappen van de Beurs vormen de Sint-Gorikshallen een gezellige plek om te ontspannen en nieuwe dingen te ontdekken, zowel overdag als bij het vallen van de nacht.\r\nDe hallen herbergen ook de Stadswinkel, een vereniging die de inwoners van het Brussels Hoofdstedelijk Gewest  wil informeren over het leefmilieu en een kwaliteitsvolle leefomgeving, huisvesting, stadsrenovatie, stedenbouw en ruimtelijke ordening, en rationeel energiegebruik. ","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"region":"brussels","backoffice_id":9562,"location":{"lat":50.84801328,"lon":4.34683241},"last_updated_at":"2024-05-08T15:56:31+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:26:22+02:00","is_in_address_book":true,"is_in_vb_export":true,"import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"resto_ranking":0},"media":[{"type":"photo","link":"https:\/\/agendabrussels2.imgix.net\/142377ccaec83dbf421781b97664e34f86024bb6.jpg","width":7952,"height":5304,"ratio":1.5,"oEmbed_height":5304,"oEmbed_width":7952,"translations":{"de":{"title":"Exposition Stoclet 1911 - Restitution @LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel Van Eetvelde","copyright":"\u00a9 Maxime Baldewyns"},"pt":{"title":"Exposition Stoclet 1911 - Restitution @LAB\u00b7AN x H\u00f4tel Van Eetvelde","copyright":"\u00a9 Maxime Baldewyns"},"en":{"title":"