/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"pt":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Guided tour of the Residence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"en":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Residence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"R\u00e9sidence Palace, the first luxury apartment complex in Brussels, was designed by the Swiss architect Michel Polak in the Art Deco style in the 1920s. It set out to be a city within the city and comprised restaurants, a theatre, a magnificent swimming pool (which should be accessible during the visits), a sports hall, a hairdresser, a bank and a post office, as well as all kinds of stores and personal services, in order to meet the needs of the members of the high bourgeoisie and aristocracy who lived there. Lacking the hoped-for success, the building was later bought by the Belgian state and transformed into administrative offices; today, it houses an international press centre.\n\nArch. Michel POLAK, 1922-1927","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/en\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"it":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Guided tour of the Residence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"cn":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Guided tour of the Residence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"fr":{"name":"BANAD Festival - R\u00e9sidence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Premier complexe d'immeubles \u00e0 appartements luxueux de Bruxelles, le R\u00e9sidence Palace fut con\u00e7u par l'architecte suisse Michel Polak, au cours des ann\u00e9es 1920, dans le style Art d\u00e9co. Il se proposait de devenir une v\u00e9ritable ville dans la ville et comportait des restaurants, un th\u00e9\u00e2tre, une piscine magnifique (qui serait accessible lors des visites), une salle de sport, un salon de coiffure, une banque, un bureau de poste, ainsi que toutes sortes de magasins et de services personnalis\u00e9s, afin de r\u00e9pondre aux besoins des membres de la haute bourgeoisie et de l'aristocratie qui y logeaient. N'ayant pas connu le succ\u00e8s esp\u00e9r\u00e9, le b\u00e2timent fut ult\u00e9rieurement rachet\u00e9 par l'\u00c9tat belge et transform\u00e9 en cit\u00e9 administrative : il abrite actuellement un centre de presse international.\n\nArch. Michel POLAK, 1922-1927","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"sp":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Guided tour of the Residence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"},"nl":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Residence Palace","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Arch. Michel POLAK, 1922-1927","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/nl\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006485"}},"place":{"id":232029,"translations":{"de":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":"Liebhaber des Art D\u00e9co sollten dieses Wohngeb\u00e4ude unbedingt einmal betreten. In der Eingangshalle sprudelt ein Brunnen aus blauen Mosaiksteinchen, w\u00e4hrend das benachbarte Restaurant mit Eleganz dekoriert ist (werfen Sie einen Blick auf die Decken!). Etwas weiter f\u00fchren pr\u00e4chtige Marmorstufen nach oben. Die in den 1920er-Jahren entworfene Anlage mutet wie eine luxuri\u00f6se Mini-Stadt an, die ihre Bewohner mit allen m\u00f6glichen Annehmlichkeiten verw\u00f6hnt. Auff\u00e4llig ist die elegante Fassade aus wei\u00dfem Stein mit n\u00fcchternen Linien, Bas-Reliefs und schmiedeeisernen Laternen.","description_print":"Liebhaber des Art D\u00e9co sollten dieses Wohngeb\u00e4ude unbedingt einmal betreten. In der Eingangshalle sprudelt ein Brunnen aus blauen Mosaiksteinchen, w\u00e4hrend das benachbarte Restaurant mit Eleganz dekoriert ist (werfen Sie einen Blick auf die Decken!). Etwas weiter f\u00fchren pr\u00e4chtige Marmorstufen nach oben. Die in den 1920er-Jahren entworfene Anlage mutet wie eine luxuri\u00f6se Mini-Stadt an, die ihre Bewohner mit allen m\u00f6glichen Annehmlichkeiten verw\u00f6hnt. Auff\u00e4llig ist die elegante Fassade aus wei\u00dfem Stein mit n\u00fcchternen Linien, Bas-Reliefs und schmiedeeisernen Laternen.","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":"Os f\u00e3s da Arte D\u00e9co n\u00e3o deixar\u00e3o de entrar neste magn\u00edfico edif\u00edcio de apartamentos para descobrir a fonte em mosaico azul-claro no hall de entrada, o restaurante decorado com eleg\u00e2ncia mesmo ao lado (d\u00ea uma vista de olhos aos tetos!) ou as escadas em m\u00e1rmores um pouco mais longe. Concebido nos anos 20 como uma mini-cidade de luxo com todo o tipo de servi\u00e7os \u00e0 disposi\u00e7\u00e3o dos seus residentes, o edif\u00edcio possui uma elegante fachada em pedra branca, com linhas s\u00f3brias, baixos-relevos e candeeiros em ferro forjado. O complexo conta com quatro alas e 180 apartamentos destinados \u00e0 burguesia \u2013 que tinha, \u00e0 \u00e9poca, dificuldade em encontrar alojamentos a pre\u00e7os acess\u00edveis \u2013 assim como um teatro de 516 lugares, banhos-turcos, salas de esgrima, cortes de t\u00e9nis no teto e uma piscina. A piscina e o teatro ainda existem, mas j\u00e1 n\u00e3o est\u00e3o acess\u00edveis ao p\u00fablico. Inaugurado em 1927, foi concebido pelo arquiteto su\u00ed\u00e7o Michel Polak. O edif\u00edcio teve uma exist\u00eancia muito curta enquanto complexo de alojamentos, uma vez que foi comprado pelo Estado belga desde 1947 e transformado em escrit\u00f3rios. Em 1988, a ala direita foi abatida para dar espa\u00e7o ao edif\u00edcio Juste Lipse do Conselho da Uni\u00e3o Europeia. O edif\u00edcio Europa, constru\u00eddo mesmo ao lado, integra uma parte do edif\u00edcio, com destaque para as escadarias classificadas. A partir de 2001, o governo belga instalou a\u00ed o seu centro de imprensa internacional, com salas de reda\u00e7\u00e3o bem equipadas, est\u00fadios de radio e de televis\u00e3o e ainda salas de confer\u00eancia. O edif\u00edcio acolhe, no r\u00e9s do ch\u00e3o, um restaurante de cozinha belgo-francesa, num enquadramento excecional.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":"Art Deco fans must visit this stunning apartment building with a sky-blue mosaic fountain in the entrance hall right next to an elegantly decorated restaurant and, a little further along, the marble stairway. Developed as a luxurious miniature city with all the services its 1920s inhabitants could need, the building has an elegant fa\u00e7ade with sober white stone lines, bas-reliefs and wrought iron lanterns.\r\n\r\nThe complex was split into four wings, housing a total of 180 apartments built for the bourgeoisie, who at that time struggled to find affordable housing in the city. There was a 516-seater theatre, Turkish baths, fencing halls, tennis courts on the roof and a swimming pool. The swimming pool and theatre still exist, but are no longer open to the public. The building, designed by Swiss architect Michel Polak, was completed in 1927.\r\n\r\nThe building\u2019s life as a housing complex was very short-lived as in 1947 it was bought by the Belgian state to be transformed into offices. In 1988 the right-hand wing was demolished to make way for the Justus Lipsius building of the Council of the European Union. Very recently the Europa building was built alongside it, incorporating a part of the building, namely the listed stairway. In 2001 the Belgian government moved their international press centre with fully-equipped editing rooms, radio and television studios and conference halls into the building.\r\n\r\nThe building houses a restaurant serving Belgian-French cuisine in a beautiful setting. \r\n","description_print":"Art Deco fans must visit this stunning apartment building with a sky-blue mosaic fountain in the entrance hall right next to an elegantly decorated restaurant and, a little further along, the marble stairway. Developed as a luxurious miniature city with all the services its 1920s inhabitants could need, the building has an elegant fa\u00e7ade with sober white stone lines, bas-reliefs and wrought iron lanterns.\r\n\r\nThe complex was split into four wings, housing a total of 180 apartments built for the bourgeoisie, who at that time struggled to find affordable housing in the city. There was a 516-seater theatre, Turkish baths, fencing halls, tennis courts on the roof and a swimming pool. The swimming pool and theatre still exist, but are no longer open to the public. The building, designed by Swiss architect Michel Polak, was completed in 1927.\r\n\r\nThe building\u2019s life as a housing complex was very short-lived as in 1947 it was bought by the Belgian state to be transformed into offices. In 1988 the right-hand wing was demolished to make way for the Justus Lipsius building of the Council of the European Union. Very recently the Europa building was built alongside it, incorporating a part of the building, namely the listed stairway. In 2001 the Belgian government moved their international press centre with fully-equipped editing rooms, radio and television studios and conference halls into the building.\r\n\r\nThe building houses a restaurant serving Belgian-French cuisine in a beautiful setting. \r\n\r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":"Les fans d'Art d\u00e9co ne manqueront pas d'entrer dans ce magnifique immeuble d'appartements pour y d\u00e9couvrir sa fontaine en mosa\u00efque bleu clair dans le hall d'entr\u00e9e, le restaurant d\u00e9cor\u00e9 avec \u00e9l\u00e9gance juste \u00e0 c\u00f4t\u00e9 (jetez un \u0153il aux plafonds !) ou les escaliers en marbre un peu plus loin. Con\u00e7u dans les ann\u00e9es 20 comme une mini-ville de luxe mettant toutes sortes de services \u00e0 la disposition de ses r\u00e9sidents, le b\u00e2timent poss\u00e8de une \u00e9l\u00e9gante fa\u00e7ade en pierre blanche aux lignes sobres, des bas-reliefs et des lampadaires en fer forg\u00e9.\r\n\r\nLe complexe comptait quatre ailes et 180 appartements destin\u00e9s \u00e0 la bourgeoisie \u2013 qui avait alors du mal \u00e0 trouver des logements \u00e0 prix abordable \u2013 ainsi qu'un th\u00e9\u00e2tre de 516 places, des bains turcs, des salles d'escrime, des courts de tennis sur le toit et une piscine. La piscine et le th\u00e9\u00e2tre existent encore, mais ne sont plus accessibles au public. Inaugur\u00e9 en 1927, il a \u00e9t\u00e9 con\u00e7u par l'architecte suisse Michel Polak.\r\n\r\nLe b\u00e2timent a eu une tr\u00e8s br\u00e8ve existence en tant que complexe de logements, car il a \u00e9t\u00e9 rachet\u00e9 par l'\u00c9tat belge d\u00e8s 1947 et transform\u00e9 en bureaux. En 1988, l'aile droite a \u00e9t\u00e9 abattue afin de faire de la place pour le b\u00e2timent Juste Lipse du Conseil de l'Union europ\u00e9enne. Le b\u00e2timent Europa, construit juste \u00e0 c\u00f4t\u00e9, int\u00e8gre une partie du b\u00e2timent, et notamment les escaliers class\u00e9s. \u00c0 partir de 2001, le gouvernement belge y a \u00e9galement install\u00e9 son centre de presse international avec des salles de r\u00e9daction bien \u00e9quip\u00e9es, des studios de radio et de t\u00e9l\u00e9vision ainsi que des salles de conf\u00e9rence. \r\n\r\nLe b\u00e2timent h\u00e9berge au rez-de-chauss\u00e9e un restaurant de cuisine belgo-fran\u00e7aise dans un cadre exceptionnel. \r\n","description_print":"Les fans d'Art d\u00e9co ne manqueront pas d'entrer dans ce magnifique immeuble d'appartements pour y d\u00e9couvrir sa fontaine en mosa\u00efque bleu clair dans le hall d'entr\u00e9e, le restaurant d\u00e9cor\u00e9 avec \u00e9l\u00e9gance juste \u00e0 c\u00f4t\u00e9 (jetez un \u0153il aux plafonds !) ou les escaliers en marbre un peu plus loin. Con\u00e7u dans les ann\u00e9es 20 comme une mini-ville de luxe mettant toutes sortes de services \u00e0 la disposition de ses r\u00e9sidents, le b\u00e2timent poss\u00e8de une \u00e9l\u00e9gante fa\u00e7ade en pierre blanche aux lignes sobres, des bas-reliefs et des lampadaires en fer forg\u00e9.\r\n\r\nLe complexe comptait quatre ailes et 180 appartements destin\u00e9s \u00e0 la bourgeoisie \u2013 qui avait alors du mal \u00e0 trouver des logements \u00e0 prix abordable \u2013 ainsi qu'un th\u00e9\u00e2tre de 516 places, des bains turcs, des salles d'escrime, des courts de tennis sur le toit et une piscine. La piscine et le th\u00e9\u00e2tre existent encore, mais ne sont plus accessibles au public. Inaugur\u00e9 en 1927, il a \u00e9t\u00e9 con\u00e7u par l'architecte suisse Michel Polak.\r\n\r\nLe b\u00e2timent a eu une tr\u00e8s br\u00e8ve existence en tant que complexe de logements, car il a \u00e9t\u00e9 rachet\u00e9 par l'\u00c9tat belge d\u00e8s 1947 et transform\u00e9 en bureaux. En 1988, l'aile droite a \u00e9t\u00e9 abattue afin de faire de la place pour le b\u00e2timent Juste Lipse du Conseil de l'Union europ\u00e9enne. Le b\u00e2timent Europa, construit juste \u00e0 c\u00f4t\u00e9, int\u00e8gre une partie du b\u00e2timent, et notamment les escaliers class\u00e9s. \u00c0 partir de 2001, le gouvernement belge y a \u00e9galement install\u00e9 son centre de presse international avec des salles de r\u00e9daction bien \u00e9quip\u00e9es, des studios de radio et de t\u00e9l\u00e9vision ainsi que des salles de conf\u00e9rence. \r\n\r\nLe b\u00e2timent h\u00e9berge au rez-de-chauss\u00e9e un restaurant de cuisine belgo-fran\u00e7aise dans un cadre exceptionnel. \r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Rue de la Loi","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Rue de la Loi, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":"Los fans del Art Deco deben visitar este incre\u00edble edificio de apartamentos, con una fuente con un mosaico azul en su entrada al lado de un distinguido restaurante, y m\u00e1s adelante la escalera de m\u00e1rmol.  Desarrollado como una lujosa ciudad en miniatura con todos los servicios que sus habitantes de los a\u00f1os 20 podr\u00edan necesitar, el edificio tiene una elegante fachada con sobrias l\u00edneas blancas, bajo relieve y linternas de hierro forjado. \r\n\r\nEl complejo fue dividido en cuatro alas, con un total de 180 apartamentos contruidos para la burgues\u00eda, que en ese momento ten\u00eda problemas para encontrar alojamiento asequible en la ciudad. Hab\u00eda 516 plazas en el teatro, ba\u00f1os turcos, salas de esgrima, pistas de tenis en el tejado y una piscina. La pisicna y el teatro todav\u00eda existen, pero ya no est\u00e1n abiertos al p\u00fablico. El edificio, dise\u00f1ado por el dise\u00f1ador sueco Michael Polak, fue terminado en 1927. \r\n\r\nLa utilizaci\u00f3n del edificio como un complejo de apartamentos fue muy corta, ya que en 1947 fue comprado por el Estado Belga para transformarlo en oficinas. En 1988 el ala derecha fue demolida para dejar paso al edificio Justus Lipsius del Consejo de la Uni\u00f3n Europea. Muy recientemente el Edifcio Europa fue contruido junto con este , incorporando una parte del edificio, a saber, las escaleras. En 2001 el gobierno belga traslad\u00f3 su centro de prensa con sus salas de edici\u00f3n completamente equipadas, radio y estudios de televisi\u00f3n y salas de conferencias al edificio. \r\n\r\nEl edificio posee un restaurante de cocina franco-belga en un precioso establecimiento.  ","description_print":"Los fans del Art Deco deben visitar este incre\u00edble edificio de apartamentos, con una fuente con un mosaico azul en su entrada al lado de un distinguido restaurante, y m\u00e1s adelante la escalera de m\u00e1rmol.  Desarrollado como una lujosa ciudad en miniatura con todos los servicios que sus habitantes de los a\u00f1os 20 podr\u00edan necesitar, el edificio tiene una elegante fachada con sobrias l\u00edneas blancas, bajo relieve y linternas de hierro forjado. \r\n\r\nEl complejo fue dividido en cuatro alas, con un total de 180 apartamentos contruidos para la burgues\u00eda, que en ese momento ten\u00eda problemas para encontrar alojamiento asequible en la ciudad. Hab\u00eda 516 plazas en el teatro, ba\u00f1os turcos, salas de esgrima, pistas de tenis en el tejado y una piscina. La pisicna y el teatro todav\u00eda existen, pero ya no est\u00e1n abiertos al p\u00fablico. El edificio, dise\u00f1ado por el dise\u00f1ador sueco Michael Polak, fue terminado en 1927. \r\n\r\nLa utilizaci\u00f3n del edificio como un complejo de apartamentos fue muy corta, ya que en 1947 fue comprado por el Estado Belga para transformarlo en oficinas. En 1988 el ala derecha fue demolida para dejar paso al edificio Justus Lipsius del Consejo de la Uni\u00f3n Europea. Muy recientemente el Edifcio Europa fue contruido junto con este , incorporando una parte del edificio, a saber, las escaleras. En 2001 el gobierno belga traslad\u00f3 su centro de prensa con sus salas de edici\u00f3n completamente equipadas, radio y estudios de televisi\u00f3n y salas de conferencias al edificio. \r\n\r\nEl edificio posee un restaurante de cocina franco-belga en un precioso establecimiento.  ","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"R\u00e9sidence Palace","address_street_name":"Wetstraat","address_street_number":"155","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1040","address_city":"Etterbeek","address_line1":"Wetstraat, 155","address_line2":"1040 Etterbeek","description_web":"Art decofans lopen best even binnen in dit schitterende flatgebouw met zijn hemelsblauwe moza\u00efekfontein in de inkomhall, het elegant versierde restaurant er net naast (plafonds!) of de iets verderop gelegen marmeren trappenhal. Ontworpen als luxueuze ministad met allerlei diensten voor zijn bewoners in de jaren 20,  heeft het gebouw een elegante gevel met sobere lijnen in witte steen, bas-reli\u00ebfs en smeedijzeren lantaarns.\r\n\r\nHet complex telde vier vleugels en 180 appartementen, bedoeld voor de bourgeoisie \u2013 die het op dat ogenblik moeilijk had om woningen voor betaalbare prijzen te vinden -  met een theater van 516 plaatsen, Turkse baden, schermzalen, tennisvelden op het dak en een zwembad. Zwembad en theater bestaan nog steeds, maar zijn niet meer toegankelijk voor het publiek. Het werd ingehuldigd in 1927 en is van de hand van de Zwitserse architect Michel Polak.\r\n\r\nHet gebouw was als woningcomplex een zeer kort leven beschoren, want al in 1947 werd het door de Belgische Staat gekocht en omgebouwd tot kantoren. In 1988 werd de rechtervleugel afgebroken om plaats te maken voor het Justius Lipsiusgebouw van de Raad van de Europese Unie. Zeer recent werd het Europagebouw ertegenaan gebouwd. Dat integreerde een deel van het gebouw, met name de geklasseerde trappenzaal. Vanaf 2001 installeerde de Belgische regering er ook zijn internationaal perscentrum met goed uitgeruste redactiezalen, radio- en televisiestudio\u2019s en conferentiezalen. \r\n\r\nHet gebouw herbergt op het gelijkvloers een restaurant met Belgische-Franse keuken in een prachtig kader. \r\n","description_print":"Art decofans lopen best even binnen in dit schitterende flatgebouw met zijn hemelsblauwe moza\u00efekfontein in de inkomhall, het elegant versierde restaurant er net naast (plafonds!) of de iets verderop gelegen marmeren trappenhal. Ontworpen als luxueuze ministad met allerlei diensten voor zijn bewoners in de jaren 20,  heeft het gebouw een elegante gevel met sobere lijnen in witte steen, bas-reli\u00ebfs en smeedijzeren lantaarns.\r\n\r\nHet complex telde vier vleugels en 180 appartementen, bedoeld voor de bourgeoisie \u2013 die het op dat ogenblik moeilijk had om woningen voor betaalbare prijzen te vinden -  met een theater van 516 plaatsen, Turkse baden, schermzalen, tennisvelden op het dak en een zwembad. Zwembad en theater bestaan nog steeds, maar zijn niet meer toegankelijk voor het publiek. Het werd ingehuldigd in 1927 en is van de hand van de Zwitserse architect Michel Polak.\r\n\r\nHet gebouw was als woningcomplex een zeer kort leven beschoren, want al in 1947 werd het door de Belgische Staat gekocht en omgebouwd tot kantoren. In 1988 werd de rechtervleugel afgebroken om plaats te maken voor het Justius Lipsiusgebouw van de Raad van de Europese Unie. Zeer recent werd het Europagebouw ertegenaan gebouwd. Dat integreerde een deel van het gebouw, met name de geklasseerde trappenzaal. Vanaf 2001 installeerde de Belgische regering er ook zijn internationaal perscentrum met goed uitgeruste redactiezalen, radio- en televisiestudio\u2019s en conferentiezalen. \r\n\r\nHet gebouw herbergt op het gelijkvloers een restaurant met Belgische-Franse keuken in een prachtig kader. \r\n","booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null}},"districts":{"list":[9],"translations":{"de":["Europ\u00e4isches Viertel"],"pt":[null],"en":["European Quarter"],"it":["Quartiere europeo"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Quartier europ\u00e9en"],"sp":["Barrio Europeo"],"nl":["Europese wijk"]}},"zones":{"list":[22],"translations":{"de":["Osten"],"pt":[null],"en":["East"],"it":["Est"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Est"],"sp":["Este"],"nl":["Oost"]}},"neca":null,"facebook_id":null,"backoffice_id":1010,"location":{"lat":50.84278696,"lon":4.38048269},"region":"brussels","last_updated_at":"2022-10-10T10:25:09+02:00","published_at":"2013-10-19T01:13:58+02:00","import_origin":null,"external_id":null,"is_in_address_book":false,"is_in_vb_export":false,"resto_ranking":0},"organizer":{"id":267246,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Explore.Brussels ist ein Zusammenschluss von Vereinen, die qualitativ hochwertige Stadtf\u00fchrungen in der Region Br\u00fcssel-Hauptstadt organisieren.\r\nDie Mitgliedsvereine sind ARAU, Pro Velo, Brussels Chatterguides und Arkadia. Im Jahr 2020 hat sich La Fonderie als Partnerverein angeschlossen.\r\nEntdecken Sie das UNESCO-Weltkulturerbe, Jugendstilarchitektur, die Bauwerke von Victoria Horta, Gem\u00e4lde von Magritte, Comic-Kunst von Herg\u00e9, Streetart, Europa, Bier, Schokolade oder besichtigen Sie architektonische Perlen des Jugendstils, des Art-d\u00e9co oder des Neoklassizismus, die normalerweise nicht f\u00fcr die \u00d6ffentlichkeit zug\u00e4nglich sind. Die F\u00fchrungen werden sowohl f\u00fcr Einzelbesucher als auch f\u00fcr Gruppen angeboten und reichen von klassischen \u00fcber originelle bis hin zu vollkommen neuen Konzepten und Formaten. Neben Stadtf\u00fchrungen zu Fu\u00df sind auch Besichtigungen per Fahrrad, Bus oder Boot m\u00f6glich.\r\nExplore.Brussels organisiert unter anderem auch das Jugendstil- und Art-d\u00e9co-Festival BANAD, die Brussels Biennale - Neoclassic (BBN) sowie weitere Projekte, darunter die Ausbildung von Stadtf\u00fchrern, der \u201eVerein der Freunde\u201c und der \u201eVerein der Eigent\u00fcmer\u201c. \r\n","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"pt":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"en":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Explore.Brussels is a network of guided tour associations in Brussels. This organisation includes ARAU, Arkadia, Bruxelles Bavard, Pro Velo, La Fonderie and Korei. Events are organised in co-production with these 6 companies. Individual or group tours are available on foot, by bike, by bus and by boat.  Visitors discover UNESCO heritage, Magritte, art deco, chocolate and much more. Explore.Brussels also organises Brussels festivals and other large-scale projects.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"it":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"cn":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"fr":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":"Explore.Brussels est un r\u00e9seau d'associations de visites guid\u00e9es \u00e0 Bruxelles. Cet organisme regroupe notamment ARAU, Arkadia, Bruxelles Bavard, Pro Velo, La Fonderie et Korei. les \u00e9v\u00e9nements sont organis\u00e9s en coproduction avec ces 6 entreprises  Les visites individuelles ou en groupe sont disponibles \u00e0 pied, \u00e0 v\u00e9lo, en car et en bateau.  Les visiteurs partent \u00e0 la d\u00e9couverte du patrimoine de l'UNESCO, de Magritte, de l'art d\u00e9co, du chocolat et bien plus encore. Explore.Brussels organise \u00e9galement des festivals bruxellois et d'autres projets de grande envergure.","description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"sp":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Avenue Brugmann","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Uccle","address_line1":"Avenue Brugmann, 405","address_line2":"1180 Uccle","description_web":null,"description_print":null,"booking_url":null,"sort_order":null,"virtual_visit":null,"visit_url":null},"nl":{"name":"Explore.brussels ","address_street_name":"Brugmannlaan","address_street_number":"405","address_street_box":null,"email":"info@explore.brussels","website":"https:\/\/www.explore.brussels\/fr","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1180","address_city":"Ukkel","address_line1":"Brugmannlaan, 405","address_line2":"1180 Ukkel","description_web":"Explore.Brussels is een netwerk van verenigingen voor geleide bezoeken in Brussel. Deze organisatie omvat ARAU, Arkadia, Bruxelles Bavard, Pro Velo, La Fonderie en Korei. De evenementen worden georganiseerd in coproductie met deze 6 bedrijven. Individuele of groepstochten zijn mogelijk te voet, per 