l\u2019interno"],"cn":[null],"fr":["Visites guid\u00e9es d\u2019int\u00e9rieurs"],"sp":["Visitas guiadas en espacios interiores"],"nl":["Interieur rondleidingen"]}}},"translations":{"de":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Van Eycken House","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/de\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"pt":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Van Eycken House","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/pt\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"en":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Van Eycken House","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Designed in 1933 for Andr\u00e9 Van Eycken, contractor and concessionaire of B\u00e9tons Hennebique in Brussels, this corner house forms an ensemble with the neighbouring building (192-194 Avenue Voltaire). Facing Josaphat Park, the two buildings, simultaneously erected by architect Jos Bal, share a continuous fa\u00e7ade and are connected by a decorative vertical frieze influenced by the Amsterdam School. Since the demise of Andr\u00e9 Van Eycken in 1965, the house underwent major transformations by its various owners before being sold in 2017. Passionate about the 1930s, the current owners set out to restore the original configuration, (re)dividing the house into two separate dwellings. Based on a prior historical study, they managed to recreate an Art Deco-style interior by integrating original elements, reinterpreting details inspired by other contemporary buildings, and integrating elements and period furniture from Brussels or even Shanghai. This original visit will allow you to understand the evolution and adaptation of a house in line with the way of life and tastes of its various occupants.\n\nArch. Jos BAL, 1933","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/en\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/en\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"it":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Van Eycken House","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/it\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"cn":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Van Eycken House","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/cn\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"fr":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Maison Van Eycken","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Con\u00e7ue en 1933 pour Andr\u00e9 Van Eycken, entrepreneur et concessionnaire des B\u00e9tons Hennebique \u00e0 Bruxelles, cette maison d'angle forme un ensemble avec l'immeuble voisin (192-194 avenue Voltaire). Faisant face au Parc Josaphat, les deux b\u00e2timents, simultan\u00e9ment \u00e9rig\u00e9s par l'architecte Jos Bal, partagent une fa\u00e7ade continue et sont reli\u00e9s par une frise verticale d\u00e9corative, influenc\u00e9e par l'\u00e9cole d'Amsterdam. Depuis le d\u00e9part d'Andr\u00e9 Van Eycken, en 1965, cette maison a connu d'importantes transformations au gr\u00e9 de ses diff\u00e9rents propri\u00e9taires, avant d'\u00eatre finalement rachet\u00e9e en 2017. Passionn\u00e9s par les ann\u00e9es 1930, les propri\u00e9taires actuels ont entrepris des travaux afin de restituer la configuration originale, (re)s\u00e9parant la maison en deux logements distincts. S'appuyant sur une \u00e9tude historique pr\u00e9alable, ils seront parvenus \u00e0 recr\u00e9er un int\u00e9rieur d'esprit Art D\u00e9co en int\u00e9grant des \u00e9l\u00e9ments d'origine, en r\u00e9interpr\u00e9tant des d\u00e9tails inspir\u00e9s par d'autres b\u00e2timents contemporains ou encore en int\u00e9grant diff\u00e9rents \u00e9l\u00e9ments et meubles d'\u00e9poque provenant de Bruxelles ou m\u00eame de Shanghai. Cette visite originale vous permettra d'appr\u00e9hender l'\u00e9volution et l'adaptation d'une maison \u00e0 l'occupation et aux go\u00fbts de ses diff\u00e9rents occupants.\n\nArch. Jos BAL, 1933","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/fr\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"sp":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Van Eycken House","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":null,"performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/fr\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/sp\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"},"nl":{"name":"BANAD Festival - Woning Van Eycken","shortdescr":null,"longdescr":"Arch. Jos BAL, 1933","performers":null,"boxoffice_url":null,"website":"https:\/\/www.banad.brussels\/nl\/","email":"info@explore.brussels","phone_contact":"+32 2 319 50 01","phone_booking":null,"agenda_url":"https:\/\/visit.brussels\/nl\/visitors\/agenda\/event-detail.5700006633"}},"place":{"id":50002939,"translations":{"de":{"name":"Maison Van Eycken","address_street_name":"Avenue Louis Bertrand","address_street_number":"118","address_street_box":null,"email":null,"website":null,"phone_contact":null,"phone_booking":null,"address_zip":"1030","address_city":"Schaerbeek","address_line1":"Avenue Louis Bertrand, 118","address_line2":"1030 Schaerbeek","description_web